  "id": "sump",
  "note": "SUMP: a cellar bar off Kessler Street with no sign.\n\nThe tile's prose: no sign, no window, no name over the door. A steel fire door set in brick and\npainted the same brown as the brick, a bare bulb in a cage above it, and a bootprint at chest\nheight. The only advertising is what comes up through the pavement grille.\n\nSo the street face is blind brick under a stepped false front, with one door in it painted the\nwall's colour, a caged bulb over it, and the grille in the pavement beside it. There are no words\nanywhere on the building. The old model used the `divebar` arm, whose kit hung two TAVERN boards\non it, which is the one thing the prose says it doesn't have.\n\nThe bar is downstairs, so the rest is plant: an extract on the flank dripping down the brick, kegs\nand bins at the back, and vents on the roof.\n\n`ty_adequate_dk` is a plain brick. The arm's `ty_bar_a` is in the window-grid family and would\npaint the windows this building hasn't got.",
  "pal": "ty_adequate_dk",
